# Cloudflare Pages edge-redirect rules (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/)
#
# `/` → `/markets` is the canonical landing for the bare domain. Today this
# redirect is implemented client-side in `src/routes/+page.ts` (307), which
# pays a full SPA boot before navigation. When the deploy target migrates to
# Cloudflare Pages this file activates and short-circuits the redirect at the
# edge (~50 ms vs ~300–600 ms SPA hop).
#
# Current deploy target is VPS-nginx behind Cloudflare proxy; nginx does not
# read `_redirects`, so this file is inert in production for now. Keeping it
# here so the migration is one config change away. The SPA-runtime fallback
# in `+page.ts` remains the source of truth until then.
#
# Status code: 307 (temporary) so we can flip back if /markets ever stops
# being the canonical landing.
/  /markets  307
